    "dimensionSource": "English Wikipedia, \"Château de Langeais\": height 16 m, width 17.5 m, depth 10 m, average wall thickness 1.5 m (maximum about 2 m). A plan exists as Atlas Archéologique de Touraine notice 166.",
    "planClass": "well-published-survey",
    "confidence": "scholarly-reconstruction",
    "note": "The outer box and the 1.5 m average wall are the published shell. The local origin is the centre of that box. The source gives no compass bearing, so the long side lies east-west. The south door is a coarse opening on one wall, not a surveyed position, and the approach azimuth points south through its midpoint. Floors and the roof are lost, so the 16 m shell is split into two equal 8 m floors with one straight stair in the void, and the cap is flat and open. Tile is only the required roof-material label. Atlas Archéologique de Touraine notice 166 shows that a plan exists; this polygon is not a tracing of it."
  }
